-- Meal Prep recipe book — the complete live set, exported from the shared
-- Supabase project. This IS the copy of record: running it reproduces every
-- recipe, method, time and scaling flag exactly as the app shows them.
--
-- Shapes:
--   ingredients  [{n: name, q: qty, u: unit, c: aisle, f?: fixed}]
--       aisle is one of meat/veg/dairy/bakery/pantry/spices/frozen/other.
--       f: true means the quantity does not move with the serving size — the
--       litre of oil you deep-fry in, the bag of charcoal.
--   steps        ordered array of strings. The app rescales quantities inside
--       the prose alongside the ingredient table, so keep them in
--       "<number> <unit>" form. Times, °C and cm are deliberately left alone.
--   scalable     false where the quantities are not really quantities: the pap
--       guide is a ratio explainer, a mug cake is one mug and a fixed
--       microwave time.
--
-- Mild by design — no chilli — and pregnancy-friendly: cooked fish only, no
-- shellfish.

on conflict (id) do update set
  name = excluded.name, emoji = excluded.emoji, meal_type = excluded.meal_type,
  serves = excluded.serves, total_minutes = excluded.total_minutes,
  scalable = excluded.scalable, ingredients = excluded.ingredients,
  steps = excluded.steps, notes = excluded.notes, updated_at = now();

